{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChGfuQ64s1i6swRy5Empn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I approved the job. The git-solver agent can now remove and prune worktrees and delete branches, so it can clean up after a failed `mg done` or a merge conflict.\n\n- **Permissions:** the old rule that blocked every `git worktree` command is replaced by narrower blocks on `add`, `move`, `lock`, `unlock` and `repair`. That leaves `list`, `remove` and `prune` allowed. The blocks on branch delete (`-d`, `-D`, `--delete`) are gone. Every other block is unchanged.\n- **Agent instructions:** the text now matches those permissions. It adds safety rules: show what would be lost first, tag any unmerged work as a backup, prefer `-d` over `-D`, and never remove the worktree or branch the session is running in. The suggested backup tag command is allowed by the permissions.\n- **Scope:** only `agents/git-solver.md` changed, apart from the job's own files.\n\nThe developer listed a few follow-ups. None of them blocks this job:\n- Reading `git reflog` is still blocked, even though the instructions tell the agent to run it. That rule was there before this job.\n- The short forms `git branch -m/-M/-c/-C` (rename and copy) aren't blocked, while the long forms are. Also there before this job.\n- The agent's description still says it \"advises safe cleanup\" rather than doing it, which may make it less likely to be picked for these requests.\n- `docs/AGENTS.md` says git-solver gets \"the full local git toolbox\", which is still wider than what the agent file allows.\n\nThere is no `.manigot/manigot.json` in this checkout, so I compared against `main`. The verdict is committed as `[peer] verdict: approved, git-solver cleanup rights`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1395,"cache_read_input_tokens":22427,"cache_creation":{"eph